From: Procursus
Subject: [PATCH] traceroute: define the maximum IPv4 option length on Apple SDKs

Apple's SDK does not expose MAX_IPOPTLEN. IPv4 options occupy at most the
difference between the maximum IPv4 header (60 bytes) and the fixed header
(20 bytes), as defined by RFC 791. Keep the upstream value when provided.
--- a/src/traceroute.c
+++ b/src/traceroute.c
@@ -29,5 +29,8 @@
 #include <netinet/in.h>
 #include <netinet/ip.h>
+#ifndef MAX_IPOPTLEN
+# define MAX_IPOPTLEN 40
+#endif
 /* #include <netinet/ip_icmp.h> -- Deliberately not including this
    since the definitions in use are being pulled in by libicmp. */
 #ifdef HAVE_NETINET_IP_VAR_H
